END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Maynard Regional Training\, Chicago\, June 4-5\, 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260520T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260520T000000
UID:7f9504b592944c23daed9fe51b65d105@sej.org
DESCRIPTION:The Maynard Regional Training Series brings in-person\, weeken
 d-long leadership and management training to journalists across the U.S. I
 n partnership with universities\, these sessions give entry- and mid-level
  editors and managers the tools and confidence they need to traverse the c
 omplexities of newsroom leadership. Deadline to register: May 20\, 2026\n\
 nCategories: National (U.S.)\, Professional Meetings\, Workshops and Fello
 wships\, Journalism & Media
URL:https://www.sej.org/calendar/deadline-0
X-SOURCE:Society of Environmental Journalists
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SPLC's New Voices Student Leaders Institute
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260520T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260520T000000
UID:567fab2d90457402b1cbd647868a5876@sej.org
DESCRIPTION:The New Voices Student Leaders Institute is a free\, online pr
 ogram that helps high school student journalists improve leadership and or
 ganizing skills\, develop leadership roles within the New Voices movement 
 and identify the best strategies to expand student press freedom in their 
 state or community. The Institute will run half-days on July 14-16 and Jul
 y 21-23\, with additional programming throughout the school year. Particip
 ants are selected through a competitive application process\, and it's ope
 n to next year’s high school students from any state. The deadline to ap
 ply is May 20.\n\nCategories: National (U.S.)\, Workshops and Fellowships\
 , Journalism & Media
URL:https://www.sej.org/calendar/deadline-splcs-new-voices-student-leaders
 -institute
X-SOURCE:Society of Environmental Journalists
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:MDRnet Community Meeting Bay Area
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260526T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260526T000000
UID:5d1c57a3fcae2221919f900001868e95@sej.org
DESCRIPTION:The Media Resilience Network invites journalists\, freelancers
  and media leaders based in Northern California interested in joining a gu
 ided community space to reflect on trauma\, grief and burnout connected to
  media work.\n\nCategories: California\, Other Events\, Professional Meeti
 ngs\, Journalism & Media
URL:https://www.sej.org/calendar/mdrnet-community-meeting-bay-area
X-SOURCE:Society of Environmental Journalists
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Knight-Risser Prize for Western Environmental Journalism
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260602T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260602T000000
UID:cba8b8fe0682ebb7759123268d56fd51@sej.org
DESCRIPTION:Up to $10\,000 is available to support an enterprise or invest
 igative environmental story set in the western United States\, which is de
 fined as all states west of the Mississippi River\, including Hawaii and A
 laska. Applications open May 6\, and close June 2\, with a winner selecte
 d in early July 2026.\n\nCategories: National (U.S.)\, Alaska and Hawaii\,
  California\, Great Lakes (IL IN MI MN OH WI)\, Great Plains (IA KS ND NE 
 MO SD)\, Mountain West (CO ID MT NV UT WY)\, Northwest (OR WA)\, Southwest
  (AZ NM OK TX)\, Canada\, Mexico\, Awards and Grants
URL:https://www.sej.org/calendar/deadline-knight-risser-prize-western-envi
 ronmental-journalism
X-SOURCE:Society of Environmental Journalists
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Planet Forward Correspondent Program
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260608T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260608T000000
UID:f99da5cadf7f6c078e9ffa6f3838fc66@sej.org
DESCRIPTION:Planet Forward Correspondents are talented students from acros
 s the country looking to apply themselves to tell the ongoing story of cli
 mate change\, with an eye toward solutions and hope. You must be currently
